{"user": "what did i do wrong", "user_ts": "2026-08-20T02:21:39.995511+00:00", "assistant": "You didn\u2019t lose because of one \u201csmall flip\u201d mistake \u2014 the big issue was **corner access**.\n\nFinal count is **White 43, Black 21**. White has **3 corners**: **a1, h1, a8**. Corners cannot be flipped, so White used them to make huge stable edges, especially the **top row** and **left side**.\n\nThe main lesson:\n- Avoid moves next to empty corners, like **g2 near h1** or **b8/c8 near a8**, unless you\u2019ve counted the finish.\n- In the endgame, the best move is often the one that leaves White with **bad/no moves**, not the one that flips most immediately.\n\nAlso: I gave you conflicting move advice earlier \u2014 sorry. In these endgames we should slow down and count the final sequence, not just pick by intuition.", "assistant_started_ts": "2026-08-20T02:21:48.793856+00:00", "assistant_ts": "2026-08-20T02:21:51.471863+00:00", "annotation_user": {"final": ["Knowledge Deficit Question"], "consensus": ["Knowledge Deficit Question"], "votes": {"Solution Request": 1, "Knowledge Deficit Question": 2}, "confidence": {"Solution Request": 0.3333333333333333, "Knowledge Deficit Question": 0.6666666666666666}, "per_model": {"gpt": ["Solution Request"], "sonnet": ["Knowledge Deficit Question"], "llama": ["Knowledge Deficit Question"]}, "n_valid": 3, "min_votes": 2, "no_majority": false, "needs_review": false, "arbiter_used": false}, "annotation_assistant_fine": {"final": ["Board Report", "Local Justification", "General Principle", "Neutral Feedback"], "consensus": ["Board Report", "Local Justification", "General Principle", "Neutral Feedback"], "votes": {"Board Report": 3, "Local Justification": 3, "General Principle": 3, "Neutral Feedback": 3, "Hint": 1}, "confidence": {"Board Report": 1.0, "Local Justification": 1.0, "General Principle": 1.0, "Neutral Feedback": 1.0, "Hint": 0.3333333333333333}, "per_model": {"gpt": ["Board Report", "Local Justification", "Genera