{"user": "how can i play better", "user_ts": "2026-08-20T02:22:04.792431+00:00", "assistant": "To play better next game, focus on **endgame control**, not big flips.\n\nKey habits:\n\n1. **Protect corners**\n   - Corners are permanent.\n   - Avoid playing next to an empty corner unless you know White cannot take it.\n\n2. **Don\u2019t chase the biggest flip**\n   - A move that flips 6 now may give White a corner or strong edge next.\n   - Ask: \u201cWhat will White\u2019s legal moves be after this?\u201d\n\n3. **Count the last few moves**\n   - In the endgame, try to imagine: Black move \u2192 White reply \u2192 Black move.\n   - Sometimes the best move is the one that leaves White with only bad moves.\n\n4. **Use mobility**\n   - Good moves reduce White\u2019s legal options.\n   - If White has to pass, that is often very powerful.\n\n5. **Edges matter, but corners matter more**\n   - White won here because White controlled **a1, h1, and a8**, making many discs stable.\n\nSimple rule: before every endgame move, ask  \n**\u201cDoes this give White a corner or an easy final sequence?\u201d**", "assistant_started_ts": "2026-08-20T02:22:09.411262+00:00", "assistant_ts": "2026-08-20T02:22:12.725883+00:00", "annotation_user": {"final": ["Solution Request"], "consensus": ["Solution Request"], "votes": {"Solution Request": 3}, "confidence": {"Solution Request": 1.0}, "per_model": {"gpt": ["Solution Request"], "sonnet": ["Solution Request"], "llama": ["Solution Request"]}, "n_valid": 3, "min_votes": 2, "no_majority": false, "needs_review": false, "arbiter_used": false}, "annotation_assistant_fine": {"final": ["Local Justification", "General Principle"], "consensus": ["Local Justification", "General Principle"], "votes": {"General Principle": 3, "Local Justification": 2, "Hint": 1, "Prompt": 1}, "confidence": {"General Principle": 1.0, "Local Justification": 0.6666666666666666, "Hint": 0.3333333333333333, "Prompt": 0.3333333333333333}, "per_model": {"gpt": ["General Principle